    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0336" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.01/12–144</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the President </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washingon</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-01">December 1, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Special Information for the President</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">[Excerpts]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d173-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>These international developments of the past two or three days will be of
                    especial interest to you:</p>
                <p>· · · · · · · · · · · · · ·</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Tito</hi>-<hi rendition="#italic">Subasic
                    Agreement</hi>. Brigadier MacLean has told Ambassador Kirk that Mr. Churchill is
                    expected to urge King Peter to accept the agreement recently formulated by Tito
                    and the Yugoslav Premier and to send a British Ambassador to Belgrade as soon as
                    the agreement becomes effective.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> E. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius, Jr</hi>. </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
